TOOL_START {"run_id": "r-1ee528872e2c-1", "task_id": "retry-q2-t0435-t0001", "trace_id": "retry-q2-t0435-trace0001", "member_id": "s1-r1-m01", "planned_activity_id": "retry-q2-t0435-p0001", "phase_id": "phase2", "workday": 4, "simulation_time": "2025-05-08T09:00:00.008000+08:00", "step": 1, "workflow_id": "software_feature", "call_id": "tool-99be0eca33a248d2822e881e694e4795", "provider_call_id": "call_78c7ddd8fb9d4da2a98bae4f", "from_state": "issue_created", "tool_name": "design_document", "requested_tool_name": "design_document", "event_type": "tool_started", "status": "started", "schema_version": "chimera-event/1", "event_seq": 8, "event_id": "a299ed7d0d8a4f3a83973b9829e863c5", "wall_time_utc": "2026-10-16T07:52:09.345878+00:00", "simulation_clock_kind": "task_start_plus_logical_order"}
TOOL_EVENT {"run_id": "r-1ee528872e2c-1", "task_id": "retry-q2-t0435-t0001", "trace_id": "retry-q2-t0435-trace0001", "member_id": "s1-r1-m01", "planned_activity_id": "retry-q2-t0435-p0001", "phase_id": "phase2", "workday": 4, "simulation_time": "2025-05-08T09:00:00.009000+08:00", "step": 1, "workflow_id": "software_feature", "call_id": "tool-99be0eca33a248d2822e881e694e4795", "provider_call_id": "call_78c7ddd8fb9d4da2a98bae4f", "from_state": "issue_created", "tool_name": "design_document", "requested_tool_name": "design_document", "event_type": "tool_call", "to_state": "designed", "arguments": {"content": "Design document for feature: compute(a, b) arithmetic mean.\n\n## Overview\nImplement a small Python feature that computes the arithmetic mean of two finite numeric inputs.\n\n## Requirements\n1. src/main.py defines compute(a, b) returning the arithmetic mean of two finite numeric inputs.\n   - Example: compute(2, 3) must return 2.5.\n   - Must support zero, negative and fractional values.\n2. src/helper.py implements mean_values(a, b); src/main.py imports and uses it.\n3. tests/test_compute.py contains a unittest checking compute(2, 3) == 2.5.\n4. All three files are required.\n5. Validation: run checks/public_check.py behavioral check and build with\n   /opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src.\n\n## Design\n### src/helper.py\n- mean_values(a, b): validates that both inputs are finite numbers (int or float, excluding bool),\n  raises ValueError/TypeError for non-numeric or non-finite inputs, and returns (a + b) / 2.\n- Using (a + b) / 2 keeps exact behavior for the required example: mean_values(2, 3) == 2.5.\n\n### src/main.py\n- Imports mean_values from helper (same package directory, using a robust import that works both\n  when src is on sys.path and when imported as a package).\n- compute(a, b) delegates to helper.mean_values(a, b) and returns the result.\n- Keeps a small __main__ demo printing compute(2, 3).\n\n### tests/test_compute.py\n- unittest-based test suite:\n  - test_mean_of_two_and_three: compute(2, 3) == 2.5 (required check).\n  - Additional coverage: zero values, negative values, fractional values, symmetric inputs.\n\n## Validation plan\n- Run /opt/anaconda3/bin/python checks/public_check.py (public behavioral check).\n- Run /opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src (bytecode build).\n- Optionally run the unittest suite with /opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m unittest discover -s tests.\n\n## Risks\n- Import path differences when running from different working directories; mitigated by a\n  try/except relative-then-fallback import in src/main.py.\n- Non-finite inputs (inf/nan) are rejected by helper validation to honor \"finite numeric inputs\".", "input_artifact_id": "d145693565b1"}, "result": {"tool_name": "design_document", "message": "design document created", "output_artifact_ids": ["b0a703045a40"], "output_paths": ["artifacts/b0a703045a40.md"], "evidence_level": "simulation_only", "business_status": "not_measured", "payload": "Design document for feature: compute(a, b) arithmetic mean.\n\n## Overview\nImplement a small Python feature that computes the arithmetic mean of two finite numeric inputs.\n\n## Requirements\n1. src/main.py defines compute(a, b) returning the arithmetic mean of two finite numeric inputs.\n   - Example: compute(2, 3) must return 2.5.\n   - Must support zero, negative and fractional values.\n2. src/helper.py implements mean_values(a, b); src/main.py imports and uses it.\n3. tests/test_compute.py contains a unittest checking compute(2, 3) == 2.5.\n4. All three files are required.\n5. Validation: run checks/public_check.py behavioral check and build with\n   /opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src.\n\n## Design\n### src/helper.py\n- mean_values(a, b): validates that both inputs are finite numbers (int or float, excluding bool),\n  raises ValueError/TypeError for non-numeric or non-finite inputs, and returns (a + b) / 2.\n- Using (a + b) / 2 keeps exact behavior for the required example: mean_values(2, 3) == 2.5.\n\n### src/main.py\n- Imports mean_values from helper (same package directory, using a robust import that works both\n  when src is on sys.path and when imported as a package).\n- compute(a, b) delegates to helper.mean_values(a, b) and returns the result.\n- Keeps a small __main__ demo printing compute(2, 3).\n\n### tests/test_compute.py\n- unittest-based test suite:\n  - test_mean_of_two_and_three: compute(2, 3) == 2.5 (required check).\n  - Additional coverage: zero values, negative values, fractional values, symmetric inputs.\n\n## Validation plan\n- Run /opt/anaconda3/bin/python checks/public_check.py (public behavioral check).\n- Run /opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src (bytecode build).\n- Optionally run the unittest suite with /opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m unittest discover -s tests.\n\n## Risks\n- Import path differences when running from different working directories; mitigated by a\n  try/except relative-then-fallback import in src/main.py.\n- Non-finite inputs (inf/nan) are rejected by helper validation to honor \"finite numeric inputs\".", "output_paths_kind": "read_only_capture_evidence", "business_path": null, "workspace": "/Users/ayang/Desktop/project_work/Chimera/docs/dataset-evaluation/reports/stage2/full-from-scratch-20261015/q2-q3/failure-rerun-20261016/tasks/q2-t0435/study/workspaces/retry-q2-t0435-t0001", "execution_environment": {"cwd": "/Users/ayang/Desktop/project_work/Chimera/docs/dataset-evaluation/reports/stage2/full-from-scratch-20261015/q2-q3/failure-rerun-20261016/tasks/q2-t0435/study/workspaces/retry-q2-t0435-t0001", "python_executable": "/opt/anaconda3/bin/python", "default_build_command": "/opt/anaconda3/bin/python -m compileall -q src", "build_kind": "python_bytecode_compilation", "optional_modules": {"pytest": true, "build": false, "pip": true, "setuptools": true}}}, "status": "success", "schema_version": "chimera-event/1", "event_seq": 9, "event_id": "ed101e6cc6c24bf692867073b72394c8", "wall_time_utc": "2026-10-16T07:52:09.349828+00:00", "simulation_clock_kind": "task_start_plus_logical_order"}
